 "Is Bopomofo only useful if my child will live in Taiwan?": 1,
 "Not exclusively. Bopomofo is used in Taiwanese heritage schools and weekend schools across North America, Australia, Southeast Asia, and Europe. It's also the system used in Taiwanese community libraries and by Taiwan-based online tutors. Its value to any given child depends on whether their materials, tutors, and community connections are Taiwan-based.": 1,
 "Why exactly does Zhuyin have 37 symbols when Mandarin has no alphabet?": 1,
 "Chinese characters are logographic — each character represents meaning, not sound. Zhuyin is a pronunciation guide layered on top: its 21 initials (consonants), 13 finals (vowel/endings), and 3 medials (glides), combined with 4 tone marks, can represent every syllable in standard Mandarin.": 1,
 "My child is already learning Pinyin at school — should I also teach Bopomofo?": 1,
 "Some families successfully maintain both; others prefer to avoid introducing a second phonics system before the first is solid. If your child's school and home materials are Pinyin-based, adding Zhuyin is an extra commitment. If you specifically want your child to access Taiwan-published books or attend a Taiwanese heritage school, adding Zhuyin over time is worthwhile.": 1,
